                <pb facs="0350" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.61383 J 41/33</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1254</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your despatch No. 2738,
                    of January 7, 1920,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d300-f1"/> regarding the Jenkins case,
                    and enclosing a copy of a despatch dated January 1, from Consular Agent Jenkins,
                    in which he states that, in his opinion, there will be considerable delay in
                    bringing <pb facs="0351" n="251" xml:id="pg251"/> the case to a settlement. Mr.
                    Jenkins makes inquiry as to what steps he should take to obtain reimbursement of
                    the financial losses suffered by him as a consequence of his recent
                    abduction.</p>
                <p>In reply you are instructed to ascertain and report definitely what are Mr.
                    Jenkins’ views with respect to the matter of reimbursement.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A.
                            Adee</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
